        <body>
            <div xml:id="d210">

                <pb facs="0488" n="392" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg392"/>

                <head>No. 208.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wing to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Quito,
                                Ecuador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-12-12"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 12, 1873</date>.
                        (Received Jan. 19, 1874.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 354.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Herewith I have the honor to forward copy
                    and translation (1 and 2) of a recent decree of the Ecuadorian Congress, which
                    may prove interesting in view of the religious agitation now so universally
                    prevalent.</p>
                <p>It is likewise shown thereby that the papal power has lost none of its strength
                    in Ecuador, no matter how it may have fared in other parts of the world.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>RUMSEY WING.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d210-a1.xml" xpointer="d210-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
